{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"2":{"eng-name":"Prayer (Kitab Al-Salat)","ara-name":"كتاب الصلاة"}},"section_detail":{"2":{"hadithnumber_first":391,"hadithnumber_last":1160,"arabicnumber_first":391,"arabicnumber_last":1160}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":913,"arabicnumber":913,"text":"Rapporté par Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه : Le Messager d’Allah ﷺ a dit : « Pourquoi certaines personnes lèvent-elles les yeux vers le haut pendant la prière ? » Puis il a parlé plus fermement : « Ils doivent cesser de faire cela, sinon leur vue leur sera enlevée. »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari (750)"}],"reference":{"book":2,"hadith":524},"chapter":{"id":169,"ara-name":"باب النَّظَرِ فِي الصَّلاَةِ","eng-name":"Looking (Up) In The Prayer","isFirstHadith":false}}]}